  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies obligated $910M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 76 awards, with an average award size of $12M. Obligations were down 21.5% year over year. Hii Mission Technologies received the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the General Services Administration, which obligated $718M, followed by the Department of Defense at $192M. Hii Mission Technologies concentrates work in two markets: All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $515M and Engineering Services with $351M. The firm’s fiscal-year obligations show growth into FY24 and FY25 before the current-year pullback: FY21 $596M, FY22 $657M, FY23 $595M, FY24 $1.1B, FY25 $1.2B, FY26 $910M. FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and partial. The mix of agency buyers and NAICS markets indicates a portfolio weighted to professional and engineering services, with smaller amounts in aircraft parts, air transportation support, R&D, and software-related NAICS categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Hii Mission Technologies' federal business trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Hii Mission Technologies' obligations rose through FY24 and FY25 before falling in FY26. Fiscal-year obligations were FY21 $596M, FY22 $657M, FY23 $595M, FY24 $1.1B, FY25 $1.2B, FY26 $910M. Obligations fell 21.5% year over year into FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets drive Hii Mission Technologies' obligations?",
        "body": "General Services Administration and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers, with $718M and $192M respectively in FY2026 to date. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services and Engineering Services are the top markets, with $515M and $351M in obligations, respectively, followed by smaller amounts in aircraft parts, air transportation support, R&D, and software-related NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Hii Mission Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies has $910M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies received those obligations across 76 awards, with an average award size of $12M, and obligations were down 21.5% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Hii Mission Technologies?",
      "a": "General Services Administration and the Department of Defense are the primary buyers. General Services Administration obligated $718M and the Department of Defense obligated $192M in FY2026 to date, with much smaller amounts from the Department of the Interior ($443K), Department of Education ($388K), and Department of Homeland Security ($18.8K)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Hii Mission Technologies sell to the government?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies sells professional, technical, and engineering services and related work to the government. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounted for $515M and Engineering Services accounted for $351M in FY2026 to date, with additional work in aircraft parts ($29.7M), air transportation support ($12.2M), R&D ($5.3M), and software and related services."
    },
